    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "musig: Clear secrets before ARG_CHECK failures in partial_sign",
    "user": {
      "login": "fametrano",
      "id": 3296421,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjMyOTY0MjE=",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3296421?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/fametrano",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/fametrano/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "`secp256k1_musig_partial_sign` loads the two secret nonce scalars and then zeroes the secnonce, so the stack copies are the only ones left. Five `ARG_CHECK`s follow: four on NULL arguments and one, after the secret key is loaded, on the secnonce's public key matching the keypair. `ARG_CHECK` returns directly, so these exits skip `secp256k1_musig_partial_sign_clear`, which every other exit after the load calls.\n\nThis clears the nonces and the secret key before each of those checks fails. The checks and their messages are unchanged. They stay after the secnonce is zeroed because the header says the secnonce is overwritten with zeros.\n\nIt matters only when the illegal callback returns and the API is misused, the key mismatch being the realistic case. It does for these exits what #1849 did for `secp256k1_musig_nonce_gen_counter`.\n\n*Assisted-by: my usual tools (LLM, Internet, computer). Mistakes are mine.*\n",
